          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em octonions
            or
            %em Cayley numbers
            (
            %a{:href => "#Cayley1845"}> Cayley 1845
            ) form a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-associative+algebra"} non-associative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/star-algebra"} star-algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕆
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{O}
            similar to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternions"} quaternions
            but with seven
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/imaginary+number"} imaginary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/units"} units
            adjoined.
          %p
            The octonions arise from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternions"} quaternions
            in analogy – namely: by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dickson+double+construction"} Dickson double construction
            (
            %a{:href => "#Dickson1919"}> Dickson 1919, (6)
            ) – of how the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternions"} quaternions
            arise from the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
            from the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normed+division+algebras"} normed division algebras
            over the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dickson+double"} Dickson double
            of the quaternions exists, called the
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sedenions"} sedenions
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normed+division+algebra"} normed division algebra
          %p
            In continuation of how the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternions"} quaternions
            control
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+groups"} spin groups
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+spin+representations"} real spin representations
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            up to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            7, the octonions control these up to the maximal dimension 11:
          %div
