          #RealAndImaginary.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              %strong (real and imaginary octonions)
            %p
              As for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
              one says that
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  an
                  %em imaginary octonion
                  is an
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi 𝕆
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in \mathbb{O}
                  shuch that under the star involution
                  %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:StarInvolution"} (1)
                  it is sent to its negative:
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi a
                          %mo ¯
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mi a
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\overline{a} = -a
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %em real octonions
                  is an
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi 𝒪
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in \mathcal{O}
                  shuch that under the star involution
                  %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:StarInvolution"} (1)
                  it is sent to itself
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi a
                          %mo ¯
                        %mo =
                        %mi a
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\overline{a} = a
            %p
              Accordingly every octonion decomposes into a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+part"} real part
              and an
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/imaginary+part"} imaginary part
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Re
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo +
                    %mover
                      %mi a
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AA
                    %mi Im
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo −
                    %mover
                      %mi a
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Re(a) \coloneqq \tfrac{1}{2}(a + \overline{a})
                    \\phantom{AA}
                    Im(a) \coloneqq \tfrac{1}{2}(a - \overline{a})
                    \\,.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#general General
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The octonions are
              %em not
              an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} associative algebra
              %em non-zero
              octonions and the
              %em unit
              octonions form
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moufang+loops"} Moufang loops
          #Alternativity.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              %strong (octonions are alternative)
            %p
              The octonions form an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/alternative+algebra"} alternative algebra
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              By linearity it is sufficient to check this on generators. So let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mi j
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e_i \to e_j \to e_k
              be a circle or a cyclic permutation of an edge in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fano+plane"} Fano plane
              as in Def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ComponentDefinition"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi e
                              %mi i
                            %msub
                              %mi e
                              %mi j
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %msub
                              %mi e
                              %mi j
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %msub
                              %mi e
                              %mi k
                            %msub
                              %mi e
                              %mi j
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %msub
                              %mi e
                              %mi j
                            %msub
                              %mi e
                              %mi k
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %msub
                              %mi e
                              %mi i
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %msub
                              %mi e
                              %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi e
                              %mi j
                            %msub
                              %mi e
                              %mi j
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    (e_i e_j) e_j
                    \&amp;=
                    e_k e_j
                    \\\
                    \&amp;=
                    \- e_j e_k
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    \-e_i
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    e_i (e_j e_j)
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p and similarly
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi e
                              %mi i
                            %msub
                              %mi e
                              %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %msub
                              %mi e
                              %mi j
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %msub
                              %mi e
                              %mi j
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %msub
                              %mi e
                              %mi k
                            %msub
                              %mi e
                              %mi i
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %msub
                              %mi e
                              %mi i
                            %msub
                              %mi e
                              %mi k
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %msub
                              %mi e
                              %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi e
                              %mi i
                            %msub
                              %mi e
                              %mi j
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    (e_i e_i ) e_j
                    \&amp;=
                    \- e_j
                    \\\
                    \&amp;=
                    \- e_k e_i
                    \\\
                    \&amp;=
                    e_i e_k
                    \\\
                    \&amp;=
                    e_i (e_i e_j)
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,.
          %h3#automorphisms Automorphisms
          #AutomorphismsOfOctonionAlgebraIsG2.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+group"} automorphism group
              of the octonions, as a real algebra, is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exceptional+Lie+group"} exceptional Lie group
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G%E2%82%82"} G₂
          %p
            See also at
            %em
              %a{:href => "normed+division+algebra#Automorphisms"} normed division algebra – automorphism
          %h3#left_multiplication_by_imaginary_octonions Left multiplication by imaginary octonions
          #LeftMultiplicationAction.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              Given any octonion
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi o
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} o
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi o
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} o
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi 𝕆
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi L
                                  %mi o
                          %mtd
                            %mi 𝕆
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi a
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↦
                          %mtd
                            %mi o
                            %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathbb{O} &amp;\overset{L_o}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \mathbb{O}
                    \\\
                    a &amp;\mapsto&amp; o a
                    }
            %p
              is an
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo −
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}-
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+map"} linear map
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
              of linear maps, this defines an
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associativity"} associative
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} acting
              linearly on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝕆
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{O}
          #CliffordActionOfImaginaryOctonions.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              %strong (Clifford action of imaginary octonions)
            %p
              Consider the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clifford+algebra"} Clifford algebra
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Im
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝕆
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mo −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Cl(Im(\mathbb{O}), -{\vert -\vert}^2)
            %p
              on the underlying
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+vector+space"} real vector space
              of that of the imaginary octonions (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RealAndImaginary"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inner+product+space"} inner product space
              via the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quadratic+form"} quadratic form
              given by the
              %em negative
              square norm.
            %p
              Then the operation of left multiplication on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕆
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{O}
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LeftMultiplicationAction"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation"} representation
              of this Clifford algebra on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mn 8
                      %msub
                        %mo ≃
                        %mi ℝ
                      %mi 𝕆
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^8 \simeq_{\mathbb{R}} \mathbb{O}
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              By
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/alternative+algebra"} alternativity
              (Prop.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Alternativity"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Im
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝕆
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \in Im(\mathbb{O})
              and every
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝕆
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in \mathbb{O}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi L
                              %mi v
                            %msub
                              %mi L
                              %mi v
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi a
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≔
                            %mi v
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi v
                            %mi a
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi v
                            %mi v
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi a
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                %mi v
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mn 2
                            %mi a
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %msub
                              %mi L
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %msup
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                    %mi v
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                  %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi a
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    L_v L_v (a)
                    \&amp; \coloneqq
                    v (v a)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    (v v) a
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    \- {\vert v\vert}^2 a
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    L_{- {\vert v\vert}^2} (a)
                    \\end{aligned}
          #ConsecutiveLeftActionByImaginaryGenerators.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              %strong (consecutive left action by imaginary generators is unity)
            %p
              The consecutive left multiplication action (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LeftMultiplicationAction"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e_i
              (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ComponentDefinition"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ±
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pm
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+function"} identity function
              on the octonions. Specifically, if one acts in increasing order of the labels in Def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ComponentDefinition"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi e
                          %mn 7
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi e
                          %mn 6
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi e
                          %mn 5
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi e
                          %mn 4
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi e
                          %mn 3
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi e
                          %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi e
                          %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi Id
                      %mi 𝕆
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    L_{e_7} L_{e_6} L_{e_5} L_{e_4} L_{e_3} L_{e_2} L_{e_1}
                    \\;=\;
                    + Id_{\mathbb{O}}
          .proof
            %h6#proof_4 Proof
            %p
              All the generators
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e_i
              are imaginary octonions (Def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RealAndImaginary"}
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CliffordActionOfImaginaryOctonions"}
              their left action on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕆
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{O}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation"} represents
              a
              = succeed "-action" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clifford+algebra"} Clifford algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Im
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝕆
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mo −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Cl
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 7
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl(Im(\mathbb{O}), -{\vert-\vert}^2) \simeq Cl_{0,7}
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mn 8
                      %msub
                        %mo ≃
                        %mi ℝ
                      %mi 𝕆
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{8} \simeq_{\mathbb{R}} \mathbb{O}
            %p
              By the
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "Clifford+algebra#ClassificationOverTheRealNumbers"} classification of real Clifford algebras
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Cl
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 7
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl_{0,7}
              has, up to
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irreducible+representation"} irreducible
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 8
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^8
              in both cases, and so the left action of imaginary octonions we have must be one of the two. The two irreps may be distinguished by the action of the “volume element”
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Γ
                        %mn 7
                      %msub
                        %mi Γ
                        %mn 6
                      %mi ⋯
                      %msub
                        %mi Γ
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma_7 \Gamma_6 \cdots \Gamma_1
            %p
              Hence we may check the remaining sign by acting on any one octonion, for instance on the unit
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi 𝕆
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \in \mathbb{O}
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ProductOfImaginaryOctonions"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi L
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi e
                                  %mn 7
                            %msub
                              %mi L
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi e
                                  %mn 6
                            %msub
                              %mi L
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi e
                                  %mn 5
                            %msub
                              %mi L
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi e
                                  %mn 4
                            %msub
                              %mi L
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi e
                                  %mn 3
                            %msub
                              %mi L
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi e
                                  %mn 2
                            %msub
                              %mi L
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi e
                                  %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %msub
                              %mi e
                              %mn 7
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi e
                              %mn 6
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi e
                              %mn 5
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi e
                              %mn 4
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi e
                              %mn 3
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi e
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi e
                              %mn 1
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                            %mn 1
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    L_{e_7} L_{e_6} L_{e_5} L_{e_4} L_{e_3} L_{e_2} L_{e_1} (1)
                    \&amp; =
                    e_7 (e_6 (e_5 (e_4 (e_3 ( e_2 (e_1 1 ))))))
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    + 1
                    \\,.
                    \\end{aligned}
          %h3#ElementaryTriples Basic triples
          #BasicTriple.num_defn
            %h6#definition_6 Definition
            %p
              A
              %em special triple
              or
              %em basic triple
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triple"} triple
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝕆
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (e_1, e_2, e_3) \in \mathbb{O}^3
              of three octonions such that
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi e
                          %mi i
                          %mn 2
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e_i^2 = -1
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi e
                          %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mi e
                          %mi j
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %msub
                          %mi e
                          %mi j
                        %msub
                          %mi e
                          %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e_i e_j = - e_j e_i
                  for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ≠
                        %mi j
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \ne j
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi e
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi e
                          %mi j
                        %msub
                          %mi e
                          %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi e
                          %mi j
                        %msub
                          %mi e
                          %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %msub
                          %mi e
                          %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e_i (e_j e_k) = - (e_j e_k) e_i
                  for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %mi j
                        %mo ,
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i,j,k
                  pairwise distinct.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Whitehead71"}> Whitehead 71, p. 691
            )
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              The choice of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e_1
              identifies an inclusion of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi 𝕆
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R} \hookrightarrow \mathbb{C} \hookrightarrow \mathbb{O}
            %p
              Then the choice of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e_2
              on top of that identifies a compatible inclusion of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternions"} quaternions
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi ℍ
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi 𝕆
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R} \hookrightarrow \mathbb{C}\hookrightarrow \mathbb{H} \hookrightarrow \mathbb{O}
            %p
              Finally the choice of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e_3
              on top of that induces a basis for all of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝕆
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{O}
            %p
              Once we have given the octonions their natural inner product, an imaginary octonion squares to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -1
              iff it has norm
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
          #BasicTriplesFormAutomorphism.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_6 Proposition
            %p
              The set of basic triples, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BasicTriple"}
